      datenErkl: 'This is where everything you create in fabBoard lives: your projects with questions, decisions and messages, your screenshots and the reports of the AI runs. These are ordinary files in a folder on your computer; none of it is uploaded to the internet. To back up your data, simply copy this folder.',
      ordnerErkl: 'You only need “Change data folder …” if your data should live somewhere else, for example in a cloud folder such as OneDrive so you have it on several devices. fabBoard then restarts and uses the new folder. Your existing files stay in the old place; to take them along, copy them into the new folder first.',
      impressum: 'Legal notice', impName: 'Name', impAnschrift: 'Address', impEmail: 'Email', impFolgt: 'to follow',
      impHinweis: 'The address will be added once the legal form is settled.',
      haftung: 'Liability and use', haftT: 'Important: please read before your first run',
      haftPunkte: ['fabBoard starts an AI that works on its own in your project folder: it creates files, changes them and can also delete them.', 'An AI makes mistakes. Check what it changed before you rely on it, for example texts, numbers or program code.', 'Back up your project folders regularly. Simply copying the folder is enough.', 'Only give the AI folders it may work in, and no secret data such as passwords.', 'fabBoard is free and provided without warranty (MIT licence). You use it at your own risk. No liability is accepted for damage, such as lost or wrongly changed files, to the extent permitted by law.'],
      haftOk: 'I have read the notice and taken note of the privacy policy. I use fabBoard at my own risk.', haftNoetig: 'Please confirm first that you have read the notice and taken note of the privacy policy.', dsLesen: 'Read the privacy policy',
      datenschutz: 'Privacy', dsStand: 'As of November 2026',
      dsTeile: [
       ['In short', 'fabBoard is a program on your computer. It has no user account, collects no data about you and sends nothing to the developer. There are no ads and no usage statistics (telemetry).'],
       ['Where your data lives', 'fabBoard stores projects, questions, messages and screenshots as ordinary files in your data folder on this computer. Only you have access to them. If the data folder is inside a cloud folder such as OneDrive, that service’s rules apply.'],
       ['What goes to the AI', 'fabBoard is just the go-between between you and your AI: it starts the provider’s official program on your computer, with your own sign-in. Everything you do with the AI goes directly between your computer and the provider.\nWhen you start an AI, it works with what is in your project folder and with your entries in fabBoard. The AI decides for itself which files it reads. Everything it reads is sent to its provider (for example Anthropic, OpenAI, Google or Mistral) so that it can answer. It is as if you pasted the content into their chat yourself. Screenshots you send to fabBoard work the same way. Whatever reaches the provider is covered by that provider’s privacy rules. So do not put secret data such as passwords in your project folder. If you use an AI on your own computer, everything stays on your computer.'],
       ['When fabBoard goes online', 'fabBoard itself goes online only in these cases: if “Check for updates automatically” is switched on in the settings (it is off at first), it asks GitHub shortly after starting and then every few hours whether there is a new version, and downloads it if needed. Nothing about you or your projects is sent. When you install an AI with the button, fabBoard downloads the program from the provider, and if needed extra programs such as Node.js. And when you open a link, for example to Ko-fi or GitHub, the page opens in your browser.\nWith all of these connections the other side sees your IP address, as with any website (the address of your internet connection); their privacy rules apply. The AI itself also goes online when it works for you (see “What goes to the AI”). Otherwise fabBoard does not use the internet: no ads, no statistics, no usage data.'],
       ['API keys', 'If you enter an API key, fabBoard stores it encrypted on this computer only and passes it only to the provider’s program.'],
       ['Newsletter', 'When you click “Subscribe to newsletter”, your email program opens with a prepared message to fab@fabboard.de. That is how you receive the newsletter. If you no longer want the newsletter, just write back and I will remove you from the list.'],
       ['Your rights and contact', 'Since the developer holds no data about you, there is nothing to disclose or delete there. You delete your files yourself by deleting the data folder. Privacy questions: fab@fabboard.de. Responsible: Fabian Diering (see legal notice).'],
      ],
